Memory Management always done automatically depending on approach
    - Done by JVM

Object no longer reference -> eligible for garbage collection

Newly created objects -> New Generation
    - Eden Space, slightly older into Survivor Space (s0, s1)

Older -> Old Generation

Mark -> Sweep -> Compact -> Repeat

Metaspace - Class methods are stored here
Thread Stacks - Variables stored here
Code Cache - Compiled code and compilation (Source code -> Bytcode -> Binary)
PC Registers - Program counter for threads
Native Method Stack - Native Methods

Tuning JVM parameters boost Performance
    - Xms, Xmx, GC Type

Avoid Memory Leaks
    - Release unused objects and resources

Memory Management Flow (Object Lifecycle)
    - Request
    - Use
    - Reclaim by GC
    - Memory return to system

Memory Layout
    - Stack - Local Variables, Function Calls
        - Memory allocated and deallocated automatically, fast
        - Size must be known at compile time
    - Heap- Dynamic Memory
        - Memory managed manually, slower
        - Allocated with new keyword
        - Size can be determined at runtime
    - Data Segment - Global and Static Variables
    - Text Segment - Code / Instructions

